it's the fourth cabinet in seven months  the government awaits congressional  approval on tuesday but it won't be easy  some lawmakers say they will not give  the new ministers a vote of confidence  unless prime minister aniwa torres makes  changes  [Music]  starting with firing the new health  minister hernan condori a doctor accused  of corruption and lack of experience  that has doctors and nurses demanding  his resignation and some of president  pedro castillo's ministers and closer  circle of advisers are being  investigated for corruption  given the accumulation of allegations  for the moral health of the republic the  president should come to congress to  answer our questions about all this  castillo himself is being investigated  since january for corruption and illegal  influence the president denies any  wrongdoing  they lie in the media saying he's  already going to resign he's corrupt i'm  not going to run away because a tiny  group of people wants to disregard the  will of the people who've put me in  office  [Music]  hours before tuesday's session his  allies had been unable to secure enough  votes for the new cabinet  i am afraid that peruvian politics  rather than seeking consensus is  dominated by short-term calculations  linked to immediate interests  many say the opposition's most pressing  interest now is paving the way for a new  ballgame  whether congress approves the new  cabinet or not critics say the real  endgame for opposition lawmakers is to  oust president castillo  a motion to unseat the president is in  the works it's the second time political  foes tried to impeach castillo but  analysts say they still don't have  enough votes to begin the process  that doesn't mean this is the end we  will surely see discussions on how to  eventually push for the president's  removal from office  a recent opinion poll suggests more than  60 percent disapprove of castillo and 77  percent disapprove of congress  from crisis to crisis the spiraling  political chaos has left the country  with five precedents in six years nearly  30 ministers were placed since last  august  disenchanted with peru's political class  for most peruvians tuesday's vote may  not make much of a difference mariana  sanchez al jazeera lima peru
 

